tests/test_link_scan_payload.py:
- encode -> UDP -> decode roundtrip over the fake-ESP32 pattern
  (tests/test_link.py): int8 negative angles, -128 sentinel,
  range_mm=4000, status 0xFE, all flag combos, exact sample equality
- a 181-sample scan tiled over three datagrams reassembles complete
  with [-90, +90] covered
- one telemetry() drain handles both a JSON telemetry packet and a
  binary chunk (each on its own path)
- regression: the exact check_parser.py bytes (v6 §2.5) no longer
  raise out of telemetry(); they are counted as rejected scan traffic,
  Hardware is untouched, and a later JSON packet still parses
- strict-decode rejects: truncation, trailing bytes, version 2,
  reserved bit 7, angle +100, range 5000, n_samples > 64

tests/test_scan_chunk_limits.py:
- chunk_count == ceil(N/64) and contiguous tiling for N in {37,91,181}
- every datagram <= 1472 B for all flag combos; <= 512 B for the
  core/+signal variants at chunk 64 and for +ambient/+t_us with the
  §2.4 reduced chunks (62/49); the 528/656 B chunk-64 overage for
  +ambient/+t_us is pinned as the spec's own numbers
- a scan missing a chunk is reported incomplete (missing/quality) via
  assemble_scan(), via assembler timeout, and via newer-scan_id
  supersede; mixed scan_ids and lying chunk_count raise
